                <pb facs="0137" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/868: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Genoa</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Balch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-15T18:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 83 [<hi rendition="#italic">82</hi>], June 12, 7 p.m. Americans in
                    Mediterranean area have remained there despite warning they should leave while
                    there was time and the Government cannot now undertake to send additional
                    American shipping for them into the dangerous combat zone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
